            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Materials"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "300 m chunky cotton. One and a half 200 m balls, or two balls if you want to keep two colours."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each granny round adds approx. 4 cm to the diameter in chunky cotton with a 6 mm hook. 7 rounds from a central magic ring = approx. 50 cm diameter."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring (MR)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr). UK term; US equivalent is double crochet (dc). Worked in groups of 3."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "MR: ch 3, 11 tr into ring, sl st to ch 3 (12 tr). Pull tail closed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: ch 3 (counts as tr), tr in same st, ch 1, *2 tr in next st, ch 1; repeat from * 10 times. Sl st to ch 3 (12 pairs, 12 ch-1 sps, 24 tr)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 3: sl st to ch-1 sp. Ch 3, 2 tr in same sp, ch 1, *3 tr in next sp, ch 1; repeat from * 10 times. Sl st to ch 3 (12 clusters, 12 ch-1 sps)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 4: sl st to ch-1 sp. Ch 3, 2 tr in same sp, ch 1, 3 tr in same sp again (double cluster: two clusters in this sp for the first time). Ch 1, *[3 tr, ch 1, 3 tr] in next sp, ch 1; repeat from * 10 times. Sl st to ch 3 (24 clusters, 24 ch-1 sps)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rounds 5, 7: each round, work 3 tr into every ch-1 sp from the previous round, with ch 1 between clusters. Add one extra cluster into a sp roughly every 12th sp to keep the mat lying flat and to slightly increase the circumference each round. Sl st to join each round. After round 7, measure, approx. 50 cm diameter. Fasten off."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "tip"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "If the mat starts to cup (go bowl-shaped), add an extra cluster into a sp every 8th cluster on the next round. If it ruffles, skip one sp every 10th cluster."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends. The chunky cotton lies flat without extensive blocking, but a light steam press around the edge helps."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine-wash on 30°C gentle cycle. Lay flat to dry. Use a non-slip bath mat underlay on wet bathroom floors."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}